# ============================================================================
# Warm-up bot — credentials reference.  COPY, DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE.
#
#     cp .env.warmup.example .env.warmup     # .env.warmup is gitignored
#
# READ THIS FIRST, or you will fill in the file and nothing will work:
#
#   A local .env file does NOT reach the deployed edge functions. Supabase edge
#   functions read their environment from SUPABASE's secret store, not from a
#   file in this repo. `.env` here is only ever used by Vite, for the frontend's
#   VITE_* variables.
#
#   So this file is a STAGING SHEET. You fill it in, then push the values to the
#   place each one actually belongs — named per section below.
#
#   This repo is PUBLIC. Never put a real value in a committed file.
# ============================================================================


# ─── SECTION A — Supabase Edge Function secrets ─────────────────────────────
#
# WHERE THESE GO:
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets
#   or:  supabase secrets set --project-ref cdyidatkegxwhtuoqxly KEY=value
#
# Read by warmup-webhook, warmup-dispatch and warmup-drainer at runtime.

# The warm-up bot's token from BotFather. A SECOND bot — never the LMS bot's
# token. Before using it: BotFather → /setprivacy → Disable, or the bot cannot
# see group comments and the entire economy silently receives nothing.
WARMUP_BOT_TOKEN=

# A random string you invent. Telegram echoes it back on every delivery in the
# X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token header, and warmup-webhook rejects anything
# that does not match. Because that endpoint runs with verify_jwt=false, this is
# the ONLY thing standing between the ingest path and anyone who guesses the URL
# — without it a stranger could forge participants, reactions and points.
#
# Generate one:   openssl rand -hex 32
# Telegram allows 1-256 chars of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ and - only.
WARMUP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional tuning. Omit both to accept the defaults shown.
# Consecutive failures before a plugin is automatically switched off.
WARMUP_PLUGIN_ERROR_LIMIT=5
# Milliseconds before a hung plugin is abandoned so it cannot stall a dispatch tick.
WARMUP_PLUGIN_TIMEOUT_MS=5000


# ─── SECTION B — injected automatically. DO NOT SET THESE. ──────────────────
#
# Supabase provides these to every edge function. They are reserved names:
# setting them by hand is at best redundant and at worst wrong after a key
# rotation. Listed only so nobody adds them "for completeness".
#
#   SUPABASE_URL
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY


# ─── SECTION C — operator credentials, local machine only ───────────────────
#
# WHERE THESE GO: nowhere. Keep them on your machine, use them, delete them.
# Never commit, never put in Supabase secrets.

# Personal access token, from Supabase → Account → Access Tokens.
# NOTE: this is ACCOUNT-WIDE. It reaches every project on the account, including
# production with the students — there is no project-scoped token in Supabase.
# Only needed if you run migrations or deploys by hand; the GitHub Actions
# pipeline already holds its own copy as a repository secret. Revoke when done.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# The LMS bot's token — needed ONCE, read-only, to record the rollback baseline
# before the config.toml redeploy:
#   curl -s "https://api.telegram.org/bot$LMS_BOT_TOKEN/getWebhookInfo"
# Do not reuse this token for anything warm-up related.
LMS_BOT_TOKEN=


# ─── SECTION D — NOT credentials. These belong in the campaign pack. ────────
#
# Recorded here only so you have somewhere to note them while setting the
# channel up. Their real home is the pack's manifest section, uploaded through
# warmup-pack-validate:
#
#   manifest.channel_id             the warm-up channel        (-100…)
#   manifest.discussion_group_id    the linked discussion group (-100…)
#   manifest.admin_telegram_ids     who may approve drafts
#
# You do not need to look these up by hand. Once the bot is admin in both, post
# a message in each and the ids arrive in warmup.events.chat_id.
#
# WARMUP_CHANNEL_ID=
# WARMUP_GROUP_ID=
# WARMUP_ADMIN_IDS=


# ─── Setup order ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Create the bot (BotFather), /setprivacy → Disable
#   2. Create the channel + linked discussion group, keep the channel PRIVATE
#   3. Add the bot as ADMIN to BOTH
#   4. Fill in Section A, push those two values to Supabase secrets
#   5. Land the config.toml commit  ← the 64-function redeploy; needs a window
#   6. setWebhook, including message_reaction in allowed_updates
#   7. Soak-test in the empty channel
#   8. RESET the warmup schema before inviting anyone — the ledger is
#      append-only, so test points cannot be deleted. See TASKS.md pre-launch.
